WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.540
Chapter five. Why prompting is dead.

2
00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.300
There was a whole industry built around prompt

3
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.300
engineering. Magic phrases,

4
00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.300
elaborate templates,

5
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:10.400
telling the model it was a world-class expert.

6
00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:12.440
All of that was a workaround for models that

7
00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:13.820
could not follow ordinary instructions.

8
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.100
They can now. That skill has quietly expired.

9
00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:21.080
What replaced it is a different job entirely.

10
00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:22.520
You stop writing steps,

11
00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:24.480
and you start stating the end state.

12
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.060
The constraints it has to work inside.

13
00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:28.960
And how you will judge whether it worked.

14
00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:31.300
Then it finds its own route,

15
00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:32.840
which is frequently a route you would not

16
00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:35.760
have chosen. Three things go into every delegation.

17
00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.480
The end state. What is true when this is finished?

18
00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.820
Something like, I can walk into the Thursday

19
00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.780
tutorial able to defend a position on this.

20
00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:47.620
The constraints. Word count,

21
00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:49.100
which sources it may use,

22
00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:51.120
the house format, what it must never do.

23
00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:52.660
Those mark the bounds.

24
00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:56.340
And the test. How will you both know it worked?

25
00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:59.240
A worked example. A check it has to pass.

26
00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.680
You already know how to do this,

27
00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:04.800
by the way. It is mission command.

28
00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:06.740
Intent, constraints,

29
00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:08.280
freedom of action, back-brief.

30
00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:11.300
The only new part is that this particular

31
00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:13.040
subordinate will never tell you when it is

32
00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:15.320
out of its depth. Which brings us to skills.

33
00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:18.980
A skill is a folder holding written instructions.

34
00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:22.920
It sits there doing nothing until a task matches

35
00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:24.440
its description, and then the model loads

36
00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:28.040
it and follows it. That is how you stop repeating

37
00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:31.120
yourself. Your standards go in once,

38
00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:32.900
and they apply every time after that.

39
00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:36.480
And the fastest way to write one is to skip

40
00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:39.040
writing it. Do a real job with the model,

41
00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:40.040
correct it as you go,

42
00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:42.520
and then say, turn everything you just learnt

43
00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.040
into a skill. It writes the file for you.

44
00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:47.600
Then cut half of what it produced,

45
00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:49.060
because it will over-generalise.

